  "conclusions": {
    "core": "No unresolved material correctness finding. Manual equipment reconciliation, finite soul-farming remediation, encounter-snapshot total-reset scaling, normal t=r rounding equivalence, v10 encounter compatibility, reset and automatic-release atomic overflow guards are source-reviewed. Final selected R19-B core/compiled bindings and fresh heldout/diagnostic actions are independently verified; no quantitative gate or denominator was relaxed.",
    "ui": "No unresolved material correctness finding. Actual correlated action results govern pending/success/rejection; stale/duplicate equipment actions are covered. Stable disclosure DOM, growth consume/restart state, tabs/codex/footer changes and field-versus-PvP preview/snapshot consumers are source-reviewed and confirmed by the final native evidence.",
    "visual": "No unresolved material correctness finding. HUD placement/animation, outlined monster numbers and head labels, current field party routing, sprite run batching and muted audio changes are source-reviewed. Historical pixel assertions retain their pixel oracle via run-strip normalization; 28 final native PNGs were inspected. Prior source-bound Chromium sprite RGBA equivalence evidence supplements the retained unit goldens.",
    "orchestration": "No unresolved material correctness finding. Current-source digest includes normative SPEC/config/protocol/source scripts and excludes generated receipts, avoiding metadata loops. Versioned task claims, literal AC commands, independent author scope requirements, source-bound native traces and same-observer performance protocol remain intact. Release runner binds successful smoke/mac/windows commands and artifact hashes to an unchanged source. Existing CURRENT v3 and v10 remain preserved; final task is excluded from its own receipt prerequisite."
  },
